      "writtenOn": "2019-10-30T09:22:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Variant and ApexType may overlap. But they have different purpose.\n- Variant determines variant name and, more importantly, tells if this variant is \"default or primary\" one. Variant \u003d\u003d \"\" means that this is a primary variant.\n- ApexType means packaging type: apex, zip, flattened\n\nVariant \"\" can be packaged in zip or apex or even flattened.\n\nYeah, we could call this as suffix or whatever.",
      "parentUuid": "c2d15afb_caa17a33",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 319,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 319,
        "endChar": 23
      },
      "revId": "1c3e3d1a7f1070f873dacbc19effa50566f2ff29",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
